and Statement II are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbaa9"}, {"id": "c5cdb6", "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbaaa"}, {"id": "8a0624", "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbaab"}, {"id": "11cb03", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbaac"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbaad", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae9"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476d"], "concepts": ["60e567dd499d1e49588f9cc4"], "question": {"text": "Hex-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>-ene-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>-ol on treatment with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PCC</mi></math> gives &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&#39;. &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&#39; on reaction with sodium hypoiodite gives &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&#39;, which on further heating with soda lime gives &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&#39;. The compound &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&#39; is"}, "options": [{"id": "d11bef", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>-pentene", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbaae"}, {"id": "380c9f", "text": "proponaldehyde", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbaaf"}, {"id": "d5e2c6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>-butene", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbab0"}, {"id": "aa5e84", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>-methylpent-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>-ene", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbab1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbab2", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae9"], "topics": ["60e5678e499d1e49588f927e"], "concepts": ["6117b8e067dbe2603c3e8ace"], "question": {"text": "An organic compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> gives dark green colouration with ferric chloride. On treatment with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CHCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KOH</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;followed by acidification gives compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> can also be obtained from compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> on reaction with pyridinium chlorochromate (PCC). Identify <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "f3471e", "text": "<p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F26d6db63-d73a-4901-ac28-7b5fd4aa8135-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 419px; height: 100px;\" /></p>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbab3"}, {"id": "8053cc", "text": "<p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Ff0caac8b-9df7-44c9-9820-9b4e61157f0e-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 390px; height: 100px;\" /></p>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbab4"}, {"id": "fd52d1", "text": "<p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F9926bf0a-8ed3-4825-b786-a161ad2bc33a-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 342px; height: 100px;\" /></p>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbab5"}, {"id": "538ec9", "text": "<p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F3ae97588-7b94-4cd4-ba6a-bf74afbae22b-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 100px;\" /></p>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbab6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbab7", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae9"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476d"], "concepts": ["6162fbf46ed13040ec854fb6"], "question": {"text": "Consider the following reactions:<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fc2b55cf6-f0b9-46c9-ae0f-9ea80ec72032-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 126px;\" /><br />&lsquo;A&rsquo; is:"}, "options": [{"id": "7eb458", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbab8"}, {"id": "e0cf3a", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>≡</mo><mi mathvaria