": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbabf"}, {"id": "3fe0a1", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F462e3ce9-f54b-4651-a773-f25618049709-image33.png?alt=media\">", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbac0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbac1", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae9"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476d"], "concepts": ["60ced3320e34b73944ddfa90"], "question": {"text": "A toxic compound \" A \" when reacted with NaCN in aqueous acidic medium yields an edible cooking component and food preservative ' $B$ '. \" $B$ \" is converted to \"C\" by diborane and can be used as an additive to petrol to reduce emission. \"C\" upon reaction with oleum at $140^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ yields an inhalable anesthetic \"D\". Identify \"A\", \"B\", \"C\" and \"D\", respectively."}, "options": [{"id": "c3944f", "text": "Methanol; formaldehyde; methyl chloride; chloroform", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbac2"}, {"id": "85e5c2", "text": "Ethanol; acetonitrile; ethylamine; ethylene", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbac3"}, {"id": "169db6", "text": "Methanol; acetic acid; ethanol; diethyl ether", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbac4"}, {"id": "a4c2f0", "text": "Acetaldehyde;2- hydroxypropanoic acid; propanoic acid; dipropyl ether", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbac5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4d5dcf815cd79dbac6", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae9"], "topics": ["60e5678e499d1e49588f927e"], "concepts": ["6117b8e067dbe2603c3e8ace"], "question": {"text": "<p>Match List-I with List-II</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>List-I</strong></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</td>\t\